   "notes": "All four terminals sit at mains potential, so all four blocks are drawn in mains red - there is no safe terminal on this module. Pins are at the wire throat under each screw, on the bottom outer edge (y=h). Terminal order left to right is AC IN L, AC IN N, AC OUT L, AC OUT N, matching hardware/BOM.csv KA1. Two facts a router must respect and the picture cannot show: AC IN L is the unit's own supply as well as the line side of its relay, so it is live whenever the rung is live; and AC OUT L is simply switched AC IN L, with the two N terminals a bonded common bus - it is NOT a dry contact and must not be drawn as one. The 'LEARN' button is drawn because the unit must be put into momentary mode (1 learn press) before use. Marking text T90 / 40A 250VAC follows the BOM's '30 A rated on a 40 A relay'; if a photograph of the actual can shows different text, correct it here rather than on a sheet."
