   "notes": "Drawn as the A202C FAMILY, three power pairs as briefed: L1/L2/L3 down the left edge, T1/T2/T3 down the right, coil A1/A2 on the bottom edge. Two things the caller should know before placing it. (1) The unit on this saw is recorded as 2-pole (ARCHITECTURE.md, Class A200, NEMA Size 1, 30 A open, 600 V, date code 1/85), so L3/T3 exist on this art but must be left unrouted on any sheet of THIS machine - or the family art gets swapped for a 2-pole variant. (2) The coil terminals are drawn in copper, deliberately NOT in the low-voltage colour: the A202C's coil voltage has not been read off the coil label (hardware/README.md open question, BUILD-LOG.md 'to confirm'), and colouring an unmeasured coil circuit as low-voltage would tell someone it is safe to touch when it may be at line voltage. Re-colour only once the label is read. Power terminals are mains red; every one of the six is live with the disconnect closed, and per BUILD-LOG the accessory receptacle is fed ahead of this device, so dropping the contactor does not make the enclosure dead. All eight pins sit on the outer edge at the screw throats."
